52365 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bcdee848-1598-5289-b462-0d40568a03c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552459 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting {{field-3}} into $\\text{L1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77948b35-77f3-58cd-80e2-2c25a0aff174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552459 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552530 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186552532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552530 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "05075f15-5b66-59aa-85c7-2761de8fc384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552530 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186311739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552532 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "092c6a00-72eb-562b-a6ec-edba31e0a817" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552532 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186396972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552554 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186552559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552554 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e6e22b3-4760-5866-a573-0523c5c9013b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552554 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552559 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186552603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552559 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5095702a-0e43-5e39-ba55-42ec3c14effd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552559 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552603 #